SUMMARY:New Moon Circle for All with Marian Noble
DESCRIPTION:Awakening Asheville\nJoin us for a welcoming and inclusive New
  Moon Circle\, where all bodies and all genders are invited into sacred ga
 thering. The New Moon is the seed point of the lunar cycle\, a powerful ti
 me to pause\, reflect\, and plant clear intentions for the month ahead.\n\
 nOur 90-minute circle opens with a grounding meditation to help you arrive
  fully in body and breath. We'll explore the astrological themes of this N
 ew Moon in an accessible way\, then move into heart shares\, holding space
  for one another in a supportive\, non-judgmental circle. We'll close with
  a ritual aligned with this month's lunar energy to anchor your intentions
 .\n\nYou'll leave with greater clarity\, deeper connection\, and inspired 
 momentum for the new lunar cycle. Whether you're new to moon rituals or a 
 longtime practitioner\, this circle offers insight\, community\, and renew
 al.\n\nThis month we gather under the Libra New Moon\, an invitation to re
 balance relationships\, restore harmony\, and call more beauty into everyd
 ay life.\n\nCome as you are. Everyone is welcome. Bring your friends!\n\n*
 *Details**\n\n* Sanctuary Studio\, 81 Weaverville Rd.\, Suite 2\, Woodfin\
 , NC 28806\n* Sunday\, October 11 at 7 - 8:30 p.m.\n* $22 per person. Spac
 e is intentionally limited to keep our circle intimate\, so reserve your s
 pot early.\n* Please arrive a few minutes early to settle in.\n\n**What to
  Bring**\n\n* A journal and pen\n* Any comfort items for your spot: blanke
 t\, pillow\, bolster\n* An altar item\, such as a photo\, a crystal\, or s
 omething from nature\, to help hold the imprint of our time together\n* Yo
 ur sober self. This is a substance-free gathering\, so come as your own sa
 cred being.\n* Curiosity and an open mind and heart\n\n**Our Circle Agreem
 ents**\n\n* **All are welcome.** There is no competition or hierarchy here
 . No one is above or below another. We meet as equals\, honoring the wisdo
 m within each of us.\n* **Self-awareness over judgment.** If judgment aris
 es (because we are human)\, see it as an invitation to self-reflect. We ar
 e all mirrors for one another.\n* **Confidentiality and respect.** This is
  a safe and sacred space. What is shared here stays here.\n* **Honor your 
 needs.** Move as you need to: get water\, use the restroom\, grab a tissue
 . You are a sovereign being and can care for yourself.\n* **Emotions are s
 acred.** There's no need to hold back\, apologize\, or adjust your emotion
 s to fit others. Your experience is your own medicine.\n* **Witness\, don'
 t fix.** We honor each other as whole beings\, holding space without assum
 ing needs or rushing to console. Simply witnessing is enough.\n* **Names a
 nd pronouns are honored.** Share yours if you wish. We commit to using the
 m as an expression of care\, presence\, and mutual respect.
